   "reply": "I've redone the lounge (101, about 6.5 × 4.6 m) as a warm cabin. You can see it at `/sketches/sk_kl7hjlhbra`. It's a new design over your Maple Street house, so the house itself is unchanged.\n\n- **Walls and floor:** honey-toned shiplap with dark walnut trim, over wide plank flooring in two brown tones.\n- **Fireplace:** there's now a fireplace on the east wall, and the room is arranged around it. The TV is gone because there was no room for the media console in front of the hearth. That suits a cabin, but I can put a screen on another wall if you want one.\n- **Seating:** a bouclé sofa and a tartan armchair face the fire. The colours are rust, cream and amber.\n- **Reading corner:** a velvet wingback with its own floor lamp and side table, plus two bookcases.\n- **Not applied:** the rug didn't take my larger size and stayed at 2.0 × 3.0 m. There's no throw blanket, since I only had furniture pieces to work with.\n\nI can also make it more rustic with a darker wood palette, or move the reading chair closer to the window."
