   "reply": "The house has two bedrooms, and I didn't know which one you meant. I went by size and designed the bigger one, room 107 at about 6.5 × 4.0 m. You can see it at `/sketches/sk_ogknpciab0`. It's a calm, light hotel look in the quiet-luxury style, with warm-minimal accents. The walls are soft off-white with white trim, the floor is pale oat planks, and the bed has linen. It has a king bed with a nightstand on each side, a large rug, a dresser, and a reading chair with a floor lamp by the windows.\n\n- **Smaller bedroom:** I also ran 105 (about 4.3 × 4.0 m) in the same style while checking sizes. It's at `/sketches/sk_0pc86bilnf`, and you can ignore it.\n- **Bed size:** the king bed was clamped to 2.0 m wide, so it's slightly narrower than a true king.\n- **Right-hand path:** the walkway down the bed's right side came out tight, and the tool flagged it.\n- **Side table:** the reading chair has no side table because there was no space for one.\n- **Lighting:** there are only two light sources, the ceiling light and one lamp. I could add a third for a layered hotel glow.\n\nIf you meant the other bedroom, say so and I'll swap them over."
